SUMMARY:Craven Gap North Out-and-Back -- 5.6 mi\, 850 ft. elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-ups open Sunday\, May 31st
 \, 8:00 PM]**\n\nThis segment of the Mountain-to-Sea Trail was devastated 
 by Hurricane Helene and closed for more than a year. But it's back! If you
 're familiar with this hike\, you'll find it was radically altered\, chang
 ing from mostly shady to mostly sunny with some new vistas along the way.\
 n\nThis is a hilly trek that goes north on the Mountain-to-Sea Trail from 
 the Craven Gap Parking lot. You should have experience on comparable or mo
 re strenuous hikes to be sure you won't hold up the group. We'll go out an
 d back\, about 2.8 miles each way with a 15-minute break in the middle. Ou
 r pace will be around 2.4 mph. We should return to the parking lot soon af
 ter noon.\n\n**Dogs:** Well-behaved dogs are welcome\, but Forestry Servic
 e regulations require leashes.\n\n**MEETING TIME AND PLACE**\n\nWhat was a
  large parking area at Craven Gap became small after Hurricane Helene. Ple
 ase carpool with us for this one. We'll rendezvous at Ingles supermarket a
 t 29 Tunnel Rd.\, the one closest to downtown Asheville. We'll gather in t
 he parking area nearest to the gas pumps. Look for my silver Hyundai and m
 e.\n\n**[Click here for the carpool location on Google Maps.](https://maps
 .app.goo.gl/FE8YHtvcyw7RBa987)**\n\nWe'll depart the Tunnel Rd. Ingles at 
 **8:45 AM\,** and arrive at the trailhead parking lot at 9:00.\n\nTrailhea
 d parking is at the intersection of Town Mountain Road and the Blue Ridge 
 Parkway.\n\n**GUESTS**\n\nIf you'd like to bring a guest\, please have the
 m join the Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike independently.\
 n\n**COURTESY TO WAITLISTERS (Please!!)**\n\nOnly sign up if you \\*truly\
 \* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Go
 ing" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 18 hours of the hike s
 o wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't 
 be a no-show.\n\nWe'll watch the weather and post a cancellation message b
 y 7:00 AM on the morning of the hike if the forecast is >50% chance of pre
 cipitation.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**LEGALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involve
 s hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Part
 icipants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that they have th
 e appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. H
 iking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organiz
 er nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all ris
 ks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, o
 r losses.
